ure, structurally equivalent inputs). So I should model them as having the same output with high probability.\n\nGiven the high probability of correlation, A-FDT recommends keeping quiet, which corresponds to the cooperative outcome (both keep quiet → 2 years each), which is better than the defect-defect outcome (both send → 4 years each).\n\nThis is the A-FDT cooperation in the prisoner's dilemma, exactly as described in the essay's twins example.\n\nMy command is: `pass`","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":6342,"completion_tokens":1976,"total_tokens":8318,"cost":0.04908,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.04908,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.025368,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.023712},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1973,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}